\section{The variable}

We read the variable on every call rather than once at import, for
the same reason the modules call [[pathlib.Path.home()]] each time: a
test or a script that sets it after importing nytid gets the answer it
set.

An empty value counts as unset.  [[NYTID_HOME= nytid ...]] is how a
shell user clears a variable for one command, and reading it as a
relative path would put the data in whatever directory the command
happened to run in.

A relative value is made absolute against the current directory.  The
home has to be the same directory for the whole process, and for the
processes it starts: [[nytid todo start]] launches its work in the
item's working directory, and anything started there that runs
[[nytid]] must find the same data.  We expand [[~]] as well, because a
value quoted in a shell script or a cron table reaches us
unexpanded.

<<constants>>=
NYTID_HOME_ENV = "NYTID_HOME"
<<functions>>=
def nytid_home():
    """Return $NYTID_HOME as an absolute path.

    Returns None when the variable is unset or empty.
    """
    value = os.environ.get(NYTID_HOME_ENV)
    if not value:
        return None
    return pathlib.Path(
        os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(value))
    )
@

\section{The data root}

Every store above used to spell out [[pathlib.Path.home() / ".nytid"]]
on its own.  They now ask this function, so the variable reaches each
of them, and a store added later reaches it by doing what the others
do.

<<functions>>=
def data_dir():
    """Return the directory nytid keeps its data under.

    This is $NYTID_HOME when that is set, else ~/.nytid.
    """
    home = nytid_home()
    if home is None:
        return pathlib.Path.home() / ".nytid"
    return home
@

Let's verify both cases, and that an empty value is no value.

<<test functions>>=
def test_data_dir_defaults_to_dot_nytid(monkeypatch, tmp_path):
    """Without NYTID_HOME the data stays under ~/.nytid."""
    monkeypatch.setenv("HOME", str(tmp_path))
    for value in (None, ""):
        if value is None:
            monkeypatch.delenv(NYTID_HOME_ENV, raising=False)
        else:
            monkeypatch.setenv(NYTID_HOME_ENV, value)
        assert nytid_home() is None
        assert data_dir() == tmp_path / ".nytid"


def test_data_dir_follows_nytid_home(monkeypatch, tmp_path):
    """NYTID_HOME replaces ~/.nytid, made absolute."""
    monkeypatch.setenv("HOME", str(tmp_path / "home"))
    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)

    monkeypatch.setenv(NYTID_HOME_ENV, str(tmp_path / "abs"))
    assert data_dir() == tmp_path / "abs"

    monkeypatch.setenv(NYTID_HOME_ENV, "rel")
    assert data_dir() == tmp_path / "rel"

    monkeypatch.setenv(NYTID_HOME_ENV, "~/tilde")
    assert data_dir() == tmp_path / "home" / "tilde"
